<h2>A close, fast South Asian market</h2>
<p>Sri Lanka sits among the shortest sea routes we quote — 2–4 days from south Indian ports to Colombo. Combined with FTA-supported preferential access for many products, it's a practical, efficient market for staple commodities: dried red chilli, chickpeas, maize and lentils lead the trade in the data we've verified.</p>

<h2>Worth checking payment conditions before a large order</h2>
<p>Sri Lanka's foreign-exchange position has been under pressure at various points in recent years, which has occasionally affected how quickly importers can complete payment for larger orders. This isn't a reason to avoid the market — trade has continued throughout — but it's worth a direct conversation with your specific buyer about current conditions before committing to a large or recurring contract.</p>

<h2>FTA documentation</h2>
<p>The India–Sri Lanka Free Trade Agreement provides preferential tariff access for many qualifying goods. We supply the certificate of origin documentation needed to support an FTA claim; your buyer's customs agent can confirm eligibility for the specific product and HS code.</p>

